        <span class="section__label">Getting Started</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">How to Get Started</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Starting your custom clothing production with SDF Clothing follows a straightforward process designed to move from concept to delivery efficiently. The process begins with sharing your requirements, after which we guide you through design development, sampling, production, and delivery. Understanding these steps upfront helps you prepare the information we need for accurate quoting and efficient project execution.</p>
        
        <p>Step one is to submit your project requirements through our contact form or email. Essential information includes: your brand background and target market, product category and style preferences, design concepts or reference materials (sketches, photos, tech packs if available), fabric preferences or performance requirements, target quantity per style and color, sizing requirements (standard size chart or custom measurements), branding requirements (labels, tags, packaging), and desired delivery timeline. The more complete your initial information, the more accurate our initial assessment and quotation will be.</p>
        
        <p>Step two involves consultation and quotation. Within 24-48 hours of receiving your requirements, we schedule a consultation to discuss your project in detail. This consultation helps us understand your vision thoroughly and identify the optimal manufacturing approach (OEM, ODM, private label, or full package). Following consultation, we provide a detailed quotation including all costs, lead times, and specifications. You may request revisions to the quotation or explore alternatives to meet budget targets. We work transparently to ensure you understand all aspects of the project.</p>
        
        <p>Step three is design and tech pack development if required. If you need design or tech pack services, our team develops professional specifications based on your concepts. This typically takes 7-14 days depending on complexity. If you provide your own tech packs, we review them for manufacturability and may suggest optimizations. Once designs and specifications are finalized, we proceed to fabric sourcing and sample development. This stage ensures that production will be based on accurate, production-ready specifications.</p>
        
        <p>Step four is sample development and approval. We develop samples according to finalized specifications, typically taking 15-20 days. Samples are shipped to you for review with detailed measurement reports and wash testing results. You may approve samples as-is, request modifications, or proceed with additional sample rounds. Each sample round adds 7-10 days. We recommend thorough testing and fit assessment before approval, as sample approval commits production. Clear communication during sampling ensures the final product matches your expectations.</p>
        
        <p>Step five is production confirmation and manufacturing. Once samples are approved, we require a deposit to confirm production and initiate material procurement. Standard terms are 30% deposit with order confirmation and 70% before shipment. Production begins after deposit receipt and material availability is confirmed. We provide a production schedule with key milestones. Throughout production, we provide status updates and maintain open communication about progress. Our production management ensures your order is completed on schedule with consistent quality.</p>
        
        <p>Step six is final inspection and delivery. Before shipment, we conduct final quality inspection and provide an inspection report for your review. Once inspection is approved, we finalize packaging with your branding elements and prepare shipping documentation. Balance payment is required before release of shipping documents. We coordinate shipping according to agreed Incoterms and provide tracking information. Throughout the process, our team is available to answer questions and provide guidance, ensuring a smooth experience from concept to delivery.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

