      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order quantity for custom clothing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Our minimum order quantity for custom clothing is 300 pieces per style. This minimum allows you to access factory-direct pricing while testing market response with manageable inventory. The 300-piece minimum can be distributed across sizes within a single colorway. Lower quantities are available for sampling and prototype development at higher per-piece costs for brands requiring smaller initial runs or needing to test multiple designs before committing to bulk production.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the difference between OEM and ODM manufacturing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) means we produce clothing according to your exact specifications, designs, and branding. You provide complete design direction including tech packs, and we manufacture to your requirements. ODM (Original Design Manufacturer) means we offer our existing designs that you can customize with your branding and minor modifications. OEM is ideal for brands with established design capabilities, while ODM suits brands seeking faster time-to-market with less design investment. We offer both models with 300-piece minimums.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do you offer private label clothing manufacturing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes. We offer comprehensive private label manufacturing from 300 pieces minimum. Private label service includes producing garments with your branding, custom labels, hang tags, and packaging. We can produce entirely custom designs or adapt our existing styles to your brand identity. Private label manufacturing gives you complete brand ownership while leveraging our manufacturing expertise. We provide guidance on branding placement, label specifications, and packaging design to ensure professional presentation.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is included in your full package production service?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Our full package production service encompasses the entire manufacturing process from design concept to finished goods. Services include design consultation and tech pack development, fabric sourcing and procurement, sample development and approval, pattern making and grading, bulk production, quality inspection, packaging, and shipping documentation. Full package production is ideal for brands seeking end-to-end manufacturing support without managing multiple suppliers. We handle all coordination, allowing you to focus on brand building and sales.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do you provide tech pack development services?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes. We offer tech pack development services for brands that need professional technical drawings and specifications. Our tech pack services include detailed flat sketches, measurement specifications, construction details, fabric and trim specifications, size grading, and bill of materials. Tech pack development typically takes 7-14 days depending on complexity. Professional tech packs ensure accurate sample development and reduce sampling iterations. We can develop tech packs from concept sketches or reference samples, or work with your existing designs to create production-ready specifications.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does the custom clothing process take?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">The complete custom clothing process typically spans 60-75 days from initial inquiry to delivery for first-time orders. This includes 2-3 days for quotation, 15-20 days for sampling and approval, 30-40 days for bulk production, and 7-10 days for shipping documentation and final delivery. Repeat orders with approved designs and fabrics typically take 45-60 days. Rush production is available at 20-30% premium for urgent deadlines. We provide detailed project timelines at order confirmation to help you plan your product launches.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

